# dotenv environment variable files.
#
# The glob is deliberately wide rather than a list of known names. A stray
# .env.bak, .env.backup or .env.old holds exactly the same secrets as .env
# and is one `git add -A` away from being public — and it is precisely the
# file nobody remembers to add here, because it gets created in a hurry
# while editing the real one.
#
# .env.example is the single exception: it carries no secrets and is the
# checked-in documentation of what the app needs to run.
.env*
!.env.example

# temp directory
.temp
.tmp

# husky internals
.husky/_

# Runtime data
pids
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock

# Diagnostic reports (https://nodejs.org/api/report.html)
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json

